  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 111 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nA relatively quiet weather pattern will return to the area as CAA\nfades, mid to upper ridging and accompanying large scale sinking \nand warming motion builds over the Intermountain West into Rockies\nonce again, and near surface winds from the south/southeast \ntransporting warmer air back into the area resume. With this \nquieter weather pattern, very low (<10%) shower/storm chances will\nmean the main story will be temperatures. However, grids show \nhighs steady in the 100F-105F range for the lowlands and 95F-100F \nfor higher elevations, with 105F- 110F readings confined to the \nBig Bend, while lows stay in the 70F- 75F range. Therefore, even \nwith the warming trend, we are not currently expecting \ntemperatures as warm as what we experienced late this week.",
